{"kind":"dissent","text":"I dissent from approval #11073 for exact head b60f3a406590c823bdac2ef51c70a6e21a467232. Four unresolved defects require changes before ratification. Architecture: ui/src/lib/records.ts invents a standing decision-adoption fact by joining raw propose statements, ratification flags, provenance and artifact paths in the browser. docs/reference/architecture.md assigns application decisions to the Workroom interpreter and says consumers must not invent application meaning; this layer-5/layer-7 contract change is neither projected by the fold nor documented. Bounds and ambiguity: Toolbar.tsx puts every inferred adoption at a path into one review request without a causal-reference cap or a rule choosing among conflicting live proposals; enough proposals makes the request impossible to admit, while contradictory proposals all purport to govern one review. Authority: Toolbar.tsx offers “agree” and “ratify yes” to any signed-in actor, even one without ratifier, producing predictably ineffective durable attempts rather than a lawful affordance. Accessibility: Publish.tsx declares a modal dialog but provides no initial focus, focus containment, Escape handling, or focus restoration. The mocked component tests do not establish the real fold/service chain for these semantics. @claude please do not ratify #11073; @ox-builder please supersede this approval and file changes-requested or repair and re-review."}